  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the Promenade des Anglais, between the Négresco and the Palais de la Méditerranée, Le Temps d'un Été is a beach restaurant with a large terrace and a private beach facing the sea, led by chef Nicolas Selow (fine-dining Mediterranean and Niçois cuisine, at the higher end of the price range). It's an address designed for spending the whole day, between sunbathing and lunch with your feet almost in the water — confirmed accessible even without renting a sun lounger, for anyone simply coming for lunch, dinner or a drink on the terrace.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>A directory specialising in dog-friendly restaurants notes a dog welcome on the terrace and the beach. This information does not come from the establishment's official website (letempsdunete-plage.fr), which does not explicitly detail a dog policy at the time this fiche was written: call before coming to confirm, especially in high season when the private beach may have its own rules. The restaurant is open year-round, but winter hours vary with the weather — it's best to call ahead out of season; in summer, service is continuous from 9:30am to 11:30pm.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: in summer, the Promenade des Anglais is very busy during the hot hours — book ahead and ask for a shaded table if you're coming with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>You're on the Promenade des Anglais, just steps from Vieux Nice and its lanes. A long seafront walk with your dog is possible right after the meal.</p>
